body:
Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.

I've double-checked that is valid GLSL (it's accepted on Shadertoy), so it makes sense to allow it for Godot shaders.

Shader code:

```gdshader
shader_type spatial;

struct a {
	float b;
};

void fragment()
{
	a a;
	a.b = 1.0;
}
```

PS: In the future, when posting screenshots of code, please paste the code below it in a code block so it can be copied easily. This is also more accessible (e.g. to screen readers).
